## Reviewer disagreements (not applied as written)

No legal finding was rejected as wrong.

- ro-a 15 and ro-b 23 correctly describe the chopped lines, but those U+200B spacers and the Q16–Q20 body paragraphs match the Korean source. They are not a Romanian-only layout error. Turning them into headings or joining the lines fails the checker, so those fixes were not applied.
- ro-a 19. The suggested line still says „nicio recomandare, nicio recomandare din partea inteligenței artificiale”. That is the stutter the row itself names. The English notice is search ranking, endorsement, recommendation, and guaranteed visibility. The applied sentence uses „susținere” for endorsement and keeps the AI recommendation as a qualifier, with „nici” on each item.
- ro-b 8. The suggested sentence still opens with „Dacă îngrijirea era necesară … se apreciază”, which is the false condition the problem line describes. Applied as two noun phrases that „se apreciază”.
- ro-a 13. The suggested sentence drops „condițiile legale” and „termenele”. The English keeps the statutory requirements and the time limits, so they stay in the Romanian sentence.
- ro-a 7. „maltratează soțul” has no personal „pe”. Applied „îl maltratează pe celălalt soț”.
- ro-b 30. „și verificat” has no finite verb of its own. Applied „și trebuie verificat”.
- ro-b 4. „să permită și să se stabilească” does not coordinate. Applied „Actele trebuie folosite și pentru a stabili”, which is the English „the evidence must also be used to determine”.
